From a918aa09fd632ab6b67bfd244f462cdf6bbc5fbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 10:59:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add cfm_agent_v_2_2: event-context scorer (scores, never
 prices)

Implements the Job 1 / Job 2 split from the team discussion: the LLM
assesses context; a future calibration layer (plain code, fit against
quant-baseline residuals) turns scores into price effects.

Changes from cfm_agent_v_2_1:
- Scope widens from geopolitics-only to all news-visible drivers, in
  five tagged categories (geopolitical, weather, operational, policy,
  demand_expectations).
- The output contract drops the forecasts block entirely. Factors carry
  signed impact scores (-3..+3) and confidence (0..1); scenarios carry
  probability and a conditional impact score. No price field exists
  anywhere in the schema.
- Ships CfmEventScorer instead of an AgentPredictor wiring: the output
  is not a forecast, so it does not convert to harness Predictions. The
  scorer drives the same ADK machinery (verified search, skill toolset,
  Langfuse tracing) with its own bounded validation-retry loop, and
  emits a flat calibration_row() for the future score-to-price fit.

cfm_agent_v_2_0 and cfm_agent_v_2_1 are unmodified.
